TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 4
TICVAI RETAIL — BOARD 1
• Retail Store & Operational Configuration — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Retail Store & Operational Configuration Board shall provide the centralized administrative 
foundation for configuring and managing all retail operations across TICVAI.
The Board shall allow authorized users to create, configure, activate, monitor and control retail 
stores, shops, kiosks, carts, pop-up stores and other retail selling locations across multiple 
tenants, companies, parks and venues.
The architecture shall support:
Tenant Company Park Venue Retail Store Zone/Area POS/Device Sales → → → → → → →
Channel
The Board shall establish the operational structure used by all downstream Retail capabilities, 
including:
• Product Catalog
• Pricing

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 5
• Merchandising
• POS
• Inventory
• Stock Transfers
• Promotions
• Returns
• Click & Collect
• Omnichannel Commerce
• Guest Profile
• Loyalty
• Payments
• Finance
Reporting
• AI & Forecasting
Retail outlets shall not operate as isolated systems. They shall consume common TICVAI services
including Product, Inventory, Procurement, Payment, Finance, Guest, Loyalty, Promotion, 
Approval and Audit capabilities.

