• CROSS-MODULE ARCHITECTURE

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 26
Board 1 shall configure Retail operations while consuming TICVAI shared services.
The architecture should follow:
• Retail Store
• ↓
• Sales Channels & POS
• ↓
• Product / Catalog / Pricing
• ↓
• Shared Inventory Engine
• ↓
• Shared Procurement Engine
• ↓
• Shared Promotion Engine
• ↓
• Payment / Wallet / Loyalty
• ↓
• Guest Profile
• ↓
• Finance
• ↓
• Analytics & AI
This distinction is important.
For example, a store may configure:
Replenish from Warehouse A when stock reaches minimum.
But the actual warehouse stock, transfer transaction, goods movement and valuation should be 
managed by the Shared Inventory Engine.
Similarly, Retail may consume a supplier cost, but supplier quotation comparison, purchase 
requisition, PO, receiving and supplier invoice workflows should belong to the later Shared 
Procurement module.
• Recommended Retail Architecture
One architectural principle should remain consistent with what we did for F&B:
Do not build Retail as another isolated POS + stock system.
The same product sold from a Gift Shop POS, Mobile POS, Guest App, B2C website, event 
merchandise stand, or self-service kiosk should use a common commerce architecture:

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 27
Product SKU/Variant Catalog Price Promotion Channel Store Inventory → → → → → → →
Location Sale Fulfilment Return Finance → → → →
Then Retail adds its specialized capabilities such as merchandising, barcode/RFID, variants, 
returns/exchanges, store stock and omnichannel fulfilment.
This will become particularly important when we reach Shared Inventory & Procurement, 
because F&B and Retail should both consume that same central inventory/procurement 
architecture rather than maintaining two separate stock systems.

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 28
TICVAI RETAIL — BOARD 2
Product, Catalog, Pricing & Merchandising Management — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Product, Catalog, Pricing & Merchandising Management Board shall provide the centralized 
Retail product-management layer for creating, organizing, pricing, merchandising, publishing 
and controlling all retail products sold through TICVAI.
The Board shall support physical merchandise, souvenirs, apparel, accessories, toys, collectibles,
photos, personalized products, event merchandise, bundles and other configurable retail 
product types.
The core structure shall follow:
Product SKU / Variant Attributes Barcode / RFID Catalog Price Promotion → → → → → →
Eligibility Channel Store Availability Publication → → → →
The objective is to maintain one centralized Retail Product Master, while allowing different 
stores, parks, venues and digital channels to determine where, when and at what price each 
product is sold.

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 29
The Board shall integrate with TICVAI's shared:
Inventory Engine
Procurement Engine
Promotion Engine
Payment Engine
Loyalty & Membership
Guest Profile
Finance
Approval Engine
Audit Engine
Analytics & AI

