The channel changes the user experience, not the underlying commercial transaction 
logic.
This is especially important for TICVAI because a guest may purchase a product through the 
mobile app, collect it from a physical store, exchange it at another store, receive loyalty points, 
and have all of those activities remain part of one traceable transaction and guest journey.

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 93
TICVAI RETAIL — BOARD 4
Store Stock, Transfers & Operational Inventory — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Store Stock, Transfers & Operational Inventory Board shall provide Retail teams with a realtime operational interface for managing stock availability, store replenishment, transfers, 
receiving, stock counts, reservations, damaged goods, serialized/RFID merchandise and 
inventory exceptions.
Board 4 shall serve as the Retail operational layer of TICVAI's Shared Inventory Engine.
It shall not create a separate Retail inventory ledger.
The architecture shall follow:
Retail Product / SKU Inventory Item Stock Location Available / Reserved / In → → →
Transit / Damaged Retail Operation Shared Inventory Ledger → →
The Board shall support:
Retail Stores
Gift Shops

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 94
Kiosks
Mobile Carts
Pop-Up Stores
Event Merchandise Locations
Photo Shops
Online / Click & Collect Stock
Back-of-House Store Rooms
Central Warehouses
Temporary Event Stock Locations
The objective is to give Retail teams everything required to operate inventory while maintaining 
one enterprise inventory source of truth across Retail, F&B and other TICVAI modules.

