• ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
The most important requirement for Board 4 is that Development must not build a Retail 
Inventory System separate from the Inventory & Procurement module we will design later.
There should be one TICVAI Shared Inventory Engine:
• Inventory Item
• → Location
• → Quantity
• → Status
• → Reservation
• → Movement
• → Cost
• → Transaction
• → Audit
Then each operational module uses that engine differently:

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 127
Retail
SKU + Store + Sale + Return + Omnichannel Reservation
F&B
Ingredient + Recipe + Production + Waste + 86
• Rental
Individual Asset + Check-Out + Check-In
• Operations
Consumables + Equipment + Internal Usage
This is particularly important because when we start the Shared Inventory & Procurement 
boards, we should not redesign the Retail stock functionality again. Instead, those boards will 
provide the enterprise engine underneath both F&B Board 5 and Retail Board 4.
That architecture will give TICVAI one stock source of truth across the entire platform, while 
still giving Retail users a backend designed specifically for their day-to-day operational needs.

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
