• ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
Board 6 should not be developed as ten independent reporting screens.
It should sit on TICVAI's common Analytics, Forecasting & AI Intelligence Layer, the same 
underlying intelligence architecture we established for F&B.
The architecture should therefore be:
• Operational Modules
Retail + F&B + Ticketing + Inventory + Procurement + CRM + Loyalty + Resource Management + 
Finance
• ↓
• Unified Data & Analytics Layer
• ↓
• KPI / Reporting Engine
• ↓
• Forecasting Engine
• ↓
• Anomaly Detection
• ↓
• Root-Cause Analysis
• ↓
• AI Recommendation Engine
• ↓
• Simulation / What-If Engine
• ↓
• Approval & Action Engine
• ↓
• Operational Modules

TICVAI | RETAIL BACKEND STRUCTURE
FUNCTIONAL REFERENCE • 202
• ↓
• Outcome Measurement
The specialized Retail Board 6 sits on top of this common intelligence architecture.
This means TICVAI does not need one AI engine for F&B and another AI engine for Retail. The 
underlying AI and analytics architecture should be shared, while each module provides its own 
business context, KPIs, forecasting models, rules and recommendations.
• Final Retail Structure
With Board 6, the Retail backend is structured as:
• Board 1 — Store & Operational Configuration
• Board 2 — Product, Catalog, Pricing & Merchandising
• Board 3 — POS, Sales, Returns & Fulfilment
• Board 4 — Store Stock, Transfers & Operational Inventory
• Board 5 — Promotions, Omnichannel Commerce & Guest Engagement
• Board 6 — Intelligence, Analytics, Forecasting & AI Optimization
This gives us a clean boundary for the next stage: Shared Inventory & Procurement should 
provide the common enterprise backbone underneath both Retail Board 4 and the 
corresponding F&B inventory/production workflows, rather than rebuilding inventory for a 
third time.